{
  "_comment": "Field-battle doctrine per culture (#608). Each doctrine is the list of team tactics that culture registers INSTEAD of vanilla's set; the engine still picks the max-weight tactic every 5 s, so a multiplier is a preference, not a script. 'multiplier' scales the tactic's own weight (0 keeps the row but never picks it, 5 is the cap); 'minTactics' is the commander Tactics skill the side needs for the row (vanilla gates at 20 and 50; a doctrine's own tactic should stay at 0); 'side' is any (default), attacker or defender. Charge is always registered even if a doctrine omits it. 'morale' is { neverRout, bravery -30..30 }: a never-rout culture's soldiers stand at zero morale (and carries no CoordinatedRetreat row), bravery is added to every soldier's starting morale. 'aggression' is four multipliers 0.25..4 on the engine's per-soldier AI values (attack: attack-on-decide chance; shield: defend-with-shield and shield-against-missiles; shooterError: below 1 shoots straighter; chargeDistance: a rider commits to a charge from further). 'formations' maps a troop id to the formation it spawns into (Infantry, Ranged, Cavalry, HorseArcher, Skirmisher, HeavyInfantry, LightCavalry, HeavyCavalry); only a TAOM tactic that keeps that slot (MumakVanguard keeps HeavyCavalry) stops vanilla folding it back. Reloads on game restart only.",
  "_comment_ids": "Vanilla ids: Charge, FullScaleAttack, DefensiveEngagement, DefensiveLine, DefensiveRing, FrontalCavalryCharge, RangedHarrassmentOffensive, HoldChokePoint, CoordinatedRetreat. TAOM ids: ShieldWall (hold the high ground in a wall that squares up against horse, advance in a wall when attacking), TwoLineWall (the wall with a second line that commits once joined; defender, needs 80 foot), InfantryMass (numbers-scaled infantry charge), Envelop (centre plus two wings round the flanks; needs 60 foot and 1.2x numbers), CavalryDominance (cavalry leads, cycle-charges, infantry follows), EoredScreen (defender: cavalry screens the flanks then cycle-charges), ArcherRing (infantry ring around the archers, defender only, volley control), ArcherAdvance (attacker: cautious advance behind an archer line, volley control), DisciplinedLine (hold or cautious advance until joined, then the line and the charge), HitAndRun (throwing infantry closes, throws, falls back, charges when spent), MumakVanguard (attacker: the HeavyCavalry formation rides ahead; needs a routed troop). DefensiveLine, HoldChokePoint and DefensiveRing need TacticalPosition entities in the scene; DefensiveEngagement, ShieldWall, TwoLineWall, DisciplinedLine and EoredScreen use the navmesh high ground and work everywhere.",
  "_comment_culture_ids": "KEYS ARE StringIds, NOT display names. TAOM re-skins the six vanilla cultures via spcultures.xslt, which overrides <name> but NEVER the id: Rohirrim = 'vlandia', Dunlendings = 'empire', Haradrim = 'aserai', Easterlings/Rhun = 'khuzait', Barding/Dale = 'sturgia', Variag/Khand = 'battania'. A doctrine keyed on the LOTR name silently applies to nobody. Cultures without a row use 'default'.",
  "enabled": true,
  "_comment_engagement": "Distances every TAOM foot behaviour and the high-ground race decide by (metres, 0 to 500; a bad value reverts to the default with a warning). cavalryMattersMetres: enemy MELEE cavalry (a real formation, 5 riders and a tenth of ours) riding at a foot formation, or already among it, inside this distance make it square up where it stands; the square holds until they are beyond 1.5 times it, then the line forms back up and keeps its foot target. It never chases horse, and horse archers never trigger the square. 100 m is about the form-up time at horse speed; the 15 s ETA horizon keeps a walking horse formation out of it. highGroundMaxMetres: a wall or ring takes the best slope toward the enemy inside this distance, never a hill beyond it. holdWhenEnemyWithinMetres: any enemy FOOT formation inside this distance ends the march; the foot forms where it stands (horse do not end it: the wall squares up against them where it is). From the first A/B (2026-09-17): the wall walked to a far hill with the horse on it, and the foot chased every passing eored.",
  "engagement": {
    "cavalryMattersMetres": 100,
    "highGroundMaxMetres": 60,
    "holdWhenEnemyWithinMetres": 50
  },
